1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:01,890
I've been waiting for you.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,590
"I've been waiting for you"?

3
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:39,840
Waiting for what?

4
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:43,390
The hand you held me with was so warm.

5
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:45,970
I can never forget it.

6
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:51,360
You must have heard
of the suspension bridge effect.

7
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:52,270
Studies show that

8
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:55,110
if someone is scared or startled,
they might misinterpret their emotions.

9
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:57,280
I was just startled earlier
because the lights suddenly went out.

10
00:00:57,280 --> 00:01:00,360
So it was a slip of the tongue. A slip...

11
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,780
Well...

12
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:03,980
What slip of the tongue?

13
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:06,090
What exactly did you say wrong?

14
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:15,180
[Hongseok]

15
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:17,650
[Park Seonghyun]

16
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:22,950
[Shin Yongseok] [Shin Junseop] [Ha Yosep]

17
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,940
[Play Me]

18
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:39,860
Haven't you been too busy lately?

19
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:41,410
We don't even have time to meet.

20
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:44,990
The musical is keeping me insanely busy.

21
00:01:44,990 --> 00:01:47,700
What was the slip of the tongue
you mentioned?

22
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:50,210
Ah... That was...

23
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:53,380
How are things with that actor?

24
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,780
We get along pretty well.

25
00:01:57,170 --> 00:01:58,670
Really?

26
00:01:58,670 --> 00:02:00,470
That's good.

27
00:02:00,470 --> 00:02:02,760
I heard you even had conditions
to cast him.

28
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,490
Conditions?

29
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:08,180
Aren't there screening conditions

30
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:09,639
when casting actors?

31
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:12,770
Like regarding meetings
and contract duration.

32
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:15,610
Ah...

33
00:02:15,610 --> 00:02:18,900
We didn't have those this time.

34
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,240
I'm heading off.

35
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,150
Tomorrow...

36
00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:23,740
I'll come to pick you up too.

37
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:24,490
No, it's fine. I...

38
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:27,490
I'll come pick you up.

39
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:29,750
Who else will take care of you besides me?

40
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,120
Thank you.

41
00:02:54,690 --> 00:02:56,270
I've been waiting for you.

42
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:58,440
He said he has been waiting for me.

43
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,840
Why did he only say it now?

44
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:04,530
Should I ask him to go to the movies?

45
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,820
Will he be very busy?

46
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:18,140
Yihyun, want to go to the movies
with me after rehearsal today...

47
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,010
Say hello.

48
00:03:24,010 --> 00:03:26,940
This is Eden,
who will be working with you from now on.

49
00:03:27,050 --> 00:03:30,720
Hello, I'm Shin Kyungmin, playing Eden.

50
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:33,020
Please take care of me.

51
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:37,520
Ah, hello.

52
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:40,400
I'm Kang Jae-on, playing Luka.

53
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:43,190
Then today's rehearsal...

54
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,440
You two can just rehearse together.

55
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:56,670
I hadn't heard there was
a separate casting for Eden.

56
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:59,290
Did you get selected through an audition?

57
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:00,500
It wasn't an audition.

58
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,050
A friend of the director recommended me.

59
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:05,920
This is my first time acting in a musical.

60
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:08,340
Please take care of me.

61
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:11,030
"What exactly do you expect from me?"

62
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:15,980
Then Eden's emotions must be chaotic
at this moment.

63
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:18,560
Even though he doesn't remember Luka,

64
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,899
his heart is unconsciously drawn to him.

65
00:04:20,899 --> 00:04:22,360
Senior?

66
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,110
Ah.

67
00:04:25,110 --> 00:04:27,860
Yeah, indeed.

68
00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:30,070
-As for the details, we should ask the director...
-Then...

69
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:31,830
"In that case,
you might as well just leave."

70
00:04:31,830 --> 00:04:34,909
He probably doesn't mean that.

71
00:04:34,909 --> 00:04:38,500
He actually cares about Luka.

72
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:41,170
That's right.

73
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:43,830
He's actually asking Luka not to leave.

74
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:49,870
Well...

75
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,000
I'm sorry.

76
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:53,190
Huh?

77
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:54,450
What for?

78
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:57,730
I actually thought you were a parachute,

79
00:04:57,730 --> 00:04:59,770
and your acting would be mediocre.

80
00:04:59,770 --> 00:05:01,270
But you act really well,

81
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:03,670
and you're really passionate about it too.

82
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:05,940
I misunderstood you.

83
00:05:06,230 --> 00:05:09,150
No worries. But...

84
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:12,120
What's your relationship
with the director?

85
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,620
I just saw you calling him by his name.

86
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:20,140
We were... friends from high school.

87
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:22,380
So have you guys been good friends
since then?

88
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:25,630
Hmm... No.

89
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,670
We reunited working on this musical.

90
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,130
I see.

91
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:34,720
You two must be pretty close.

92
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:37,020
Since you're asking him out to movies
after the rehearsal.

93
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:40,310
Friends don't really go to movies.

94
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:42,940
Though they might go to an internet cafe.

95
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:45,610
Ah, well...

96
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:49,900
Yihyun and I...

97
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:54,909
Shall we just...
quickly finish the rehearsal?

98
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:56,830
Sure.

99
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:12,090
Hello, Mr. Yoo.

100
00:06:12,090 --> 00:06:15,350
I heard they've been friends
since high school.

101
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:17,930
But I don't know why,

102
00:06:17,930 --> 00:06:22,190
they drifted apart for a while. It seems
they got close again after working on the musical.

103
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:23,650
From what I see...

104
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,810
What?

105
00:06:24,810 --> 00:06:27,020
They don't seem like ordinary friends.

106
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:32,790
The way they look at each other
is quite intriguing.

107
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:33,980
Find a way

108
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:37,030
to break them up for me.

109
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:39,490
Yes.

110
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,500
But,

111
00:06:42,659 --> 00:06:45,250
is it necessary to go this far?

112
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:48,710
Yihyun has been hurt a lot.

113
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:50,510
He can't do anything without me.

114
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:52,130
All right.

115
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:57,100
Just do as you are told.

116
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:59,850
I really like this line.

117
00:06:59,850 --> 00:07:02,680
Also, would it be better
if I give a hug here?

118
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:07,610
How about we run towards each other
at the same time and hug?

119
00:07:08,650 --> 00:07:10,440
Sounds good.

120
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:12,110
One, two.

121
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:16,610
Wait, shouldn't this light be replaced?

122
00:07:16,610 --> 00:07:17,910
Yeah.

123
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:24,040
The floor doesn't seem very sturdy either.

124
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:26,790
D-Director?

125
00:07:27,790 --> 00:07:30,340
I'll go get a hammer and some nails.

126
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:34,670
Ah...

127
00:07:34,670 --> 00:07:37,510
I'll go with him.

128
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:45,450
This doesn't look like
they're just ordinary friends.

129
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,100
What's going on with these two?

130
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:50,440
Senior,

131
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,860
when you say this line,

132
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:54,990
how about you stand up there and call me?

133
00:07:56,030 --> 00:07:57,530
When I hear the line,

134
00:07:57,530 --> 00:08:00,130
I'll just turn around
and look at you like this.

135
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:04,890
This way there will be a height difference
in our line of sight...

136
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:05,790
I think it will be great.

137
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:07,000
Shall we give it a try?

138
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,330
Okay.

139
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:15,130
But this chair seems a bit wobbly.

140
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:17,340
Then let's just do this line.

141
00:08:18,930 --> 00:08:20,680
It's me, Eden.

142
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,310
That day in the storm...

143
00:08:27,270 --> 00:08:29,400
Senior, are you okay?

144
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,310
I'm sorry.

145
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:31,860
It's all my fault.

146
00:08:34,070 --> 00:08:35,150
Are you okay?

147
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:37,610
Are you hurt?

148
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,110
Hey, shouldn't you go to the hospital?

149
00:08:57,670 --> 00:08:59,340
How about we run towards each other
at the same time and hug?

150
00:08:59,340 --> 00:08:59,970
This light...

151
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:02,970
The floor doesn't seem very sturdy either.

152
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:06,060
Why am I like this?

153
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:20,740
I was worried you'd be injured.

154
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,370
Just put it here.

155
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,780
Will you take it off yourself,

156
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,590
or should I help you?

157
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:52,900
Let me give you a heads up.

158
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:57,650
I have nothing to do with Kyungmin.

159
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:00,540
Why bring this up all of a sudden?

160
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,660
Just in case you misunderstand.

161
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:13,750
Are you mad at me?

162
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,800
No.

163
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,210
He's probably not mad.
